A||N||14||1FST2M6||Perfect example... 2 turbos TOO small||||1||
Z||000000||1FST2M6||12-04-2000||08:52 AM||||ok this weekend i was at the shop cause of  the "Grassroots Day" that GRM puts on for the area.. you get a cheaper dyno rate when the magazine guys are there.. (they pic up the rest of the tab) this guy showed up.. 58 Mercury Voyager with a 460 and twin-turbo. he'd done all the work himself and it looks GREAT.. BUT with a 460 he needs obviously LOTS of air.. he's running 2 T3-super 60s.. which will support his car to 2700rpm then fall on it's face. at their PEAK effencincy it's making 300hp and 714lbft of torque. I've got it in mpeg form if anyone wants it.. he later that day purchased 2 T4-super 60s that will support 800+hp. i'll keep you posted.  <P><BR>anyone have the December issue of GrassRoots Motorsports? there is a big write up on all of daves Miata work.. if you look at the first pic.. thats me in the car driving it on the dyno!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> my 15min of fame. <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/58merc_side.jpg">   <P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/58merc_twinturbo.jpg">   <P><BR>oh yeah... he running 8psi at 2700rpm then it drops RIGHT the hell off.. to nearly vacuum again at it's 5000rpm redline (actually about 1.3psi)... with 8.2:1 compression, twin saab 9000 intercoolers mounted underneath each headlight behind the grill! you'll see it in marchs' Hot Rod at the Power Tour photo shoot.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Black88GT||12-04-2000||10:03 AM||||You gotta send me the MPEG!!<P>714 lb. ft. of torque?!  OMG!<P>Never gonna challenge an old '58 Voyager wagon on the streets...<BR><P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>'88 GT t-top 3.4<BR>Baltimore, MD<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/cartmanico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kennyico.gif">         <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/stanico.gif">       <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/kyleico.gif">           <IMG SRC="http://cgi.tripod.com/smilecwm/cgi-bin/s/sp/chefico.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Philphine||12-04-2000||12:00 PM||||on a guess. turbos off a couple of turbo regals should do it, if my math was right. are the turbos the same on a regal and syclone/typhoon? what about that one year turbo grand prix gtp? <P>that might be useful. a list of turbo cars (the fairly common ones you might luck across in a junkyard or ebay) and what size engine and turbo came in them.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-04-2000||12:52 PM||||Watch out when Hot Rod says your car will be in such and such date's issue. They told me my car was goimg to be in the Dec. issue now they say the May issue.||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||12-04-2000||01:25 PM||||with the exception of the turbos he ordered on saturday.. EVERYTHING came from a bone-yard.. all bits and pieces of different cars. the car itself was a one owner until about 18mo. ago when he found it. the turbos on a regal would be ok but they too would fall on their face.. about 3500.. it's a 460!! need 1100cfm to support it at 850lbft at 5000rpm thats a LOT of air!! regal units would help but wouldn't be what he wants.. which is 400ish hp and 850lbft. <P>and he has the layout already printed up and sent to him for editing. we got to see it. the first pic of the layout is his car 3/4 covered in tire smoke and the nose just sitting still..  pretty sweet!  he was trying to get the Grassroots guys to buy it and use it as a tow vehicle! ..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> they all just shook they're heads and laughed... "you don't need 700lbft to pull a spitfire"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  ||||reg||1
