Z||000010||1FST2M6||12-04-2000||04:05 PM||||I've tried!!! Been to dinner MANY MANY times with David Wallens! took him for a slide around the block a few times in the Nitrous car.. he likes  along with the Publisher Tim Suddard and editor Bob herrington but just haven't ben able to push them over the edge to say " ok.. lets do this.." <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/M3_runnin_grassroots.jpg">      <BR> <BR>Thats Tim (bent over) talking to Ed in the M3. they were trying all day to find 170hp at the wheels.. but only were able to muster 164.3 with h-pipe, Supersprint muffler and K&N cone filter... (after trying 3 different cat configurations, stock muffler, Ravin and the SS, stock air box, euro air box, K&N drop in and then the Cone filter) all day dyno research session  still 164 isn't bad for a 2.3liter 4cyl!<p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 12-04-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000011||PearlBlueSoul||12-04-2000||04:11 PM||||LOL.  OOOH trust me, I know that one.  hehe.  That's why so many people have decided to build up auto Supras instead of manuals.  Ivan can't keep a clutch or a set of tires on that car to save his life.  He seriously needs to get a triple disk HKS setup for that damn thing.  That and some super soft compound tires.   <P>Doesn't suprise me that Ivan does that.  He snagged 4th off the top of the 575 onramp (next door to McDonalds) at the top/end of the ramp.  Said it squiggled for a second, he got it back, and it literally SNAPped into traction.  Snapped so hard he slammed his head on the driver's door window and had a knot the size of a baseball on his head for a couple weeks afterwards.  Talk about traction issues!  But you're right about spending too much.  I'dve just gone out and built up a MR2 turbo with a 95-99 Jspec motor for how much he spent on his car.  sheish.  ||||reg||1
